# Repo-root .dockerignore — needed now that apps/api/Dockerfile.prod
# builds with the monorepo root as context (Railway's build context
# always matches its configured Root Directory). Without this, the
# targeted COPYs in that Dockerfile (apps/site-builder, packages/*)
# would drag along whatever's already installed/built on the host
# checkout — node_modules, .astro/.turbo caches, dist output — none of
# which should ever be trusted from outside the image (stale, and
# potentially host-arch-specific native deps); `pnpm install` and
# `astro build` regenerate all of it inside the image instead.
#
# apps/studio/Dockerfile also already builds with this same root
# context (see docker-compose.yml) and benefits from this too — it just
# never had a .dockerignore to rely on before.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.astro
**/.turbo
**/.wrangler
**/.tmp-builds
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

.git
.github

# apps/api-specific: regenerated by `uv sync` inside the image, or
# local-only dev artifacts that must never ship in an image.
apps/api/.venv
apps/api/dev.db
apps/api/.env
